# The root expression of a caos client repo: mount caos' `std/` into THIS
# tree's evaluation result, so everything below can name `caos-std/<entry>`.
#
# Nothing of caos is committed here. The mount exists only in the evaluated
# tree — content-addressed, deduped, never on disk — which is why `caos-std/`
# is gitignored and why this repo stays a handful of text files however large
# caos gets.
#
# ONE LINE, and it has to be: a directive is a line, and there are no backslash
# continuations. design/flake-inputs.md wraps this same expression across four
# lines to fit the page; copying that wrapping verbatim makes every resolution
# of `caos-std/` fail.
#
# The locator appears TWICE on purpose (design/flake-inputs.md, "Consumer
# root"): `--base` yields the loader's own image, `--input-tree` yields the
# tree it splices. Passing the tree as an argument is what lets the server's
# `:@@=` resolution fetch it before the request is keyed, so the ArgTree
# carries an oid and the URL never enters a cache key.
#
# Every rev here must equal what flake.lock locks for `--input=caos`. The
# loader checks exactly that, over all three locators, and refuses the
# evaluation if any differs.
#
# The second line resolves this repo's OWN `DEPS` files (design/flake-inputs.md:
# "the consumer's root expression chains to caos' deep-deps in a second line if
# it wants DEPS resolution too"). A tool under caos-tools/ cannot name
# `../../caos-std/go` from its own expression — an expression is evaluated
# against its own directory — so it declares the dependency in DEPS and caos'
# deep-deps worker mounts it at `DEEP-DEPS/<name>` inside the tool. The loader
# runs first so those DEPS can point into caos-std/.
LOADED=run --base:@@=github:Metta-AI/caos?rev=74d72c8f5a66a9fb81b580033b8aa24242712a76&dir=std/flake-input-loader --in:@=. --expr=$CAOS_EXPR --input=caos --input-tree:@@=github:Metta-AI/caos?rev=74d72c8f5a66a9fb81b580033b8aa24242712a76&dir=std --output-path=caos-std
run --base:@@=github:Metta-AI/caos?rev=74d72c8f5a66a9fb81b580033b8aa24242712a76&dir=std/deep-deps --in=$LOADED
